<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds were easing as profit-taking spread across European markets but the local 10 year bond was slightly outperforming the Bunds.</p>
<p>&quot;The bonds are falling in line with the general trend (elsewhere), but they are better supported than the Bund,&quot; said one trader. The yield curve was remaining steady at some 103 basis points.</p>
<p>Traders saw little on the international agenda for Friday to change the mood, with liquidity likely to remain low in view of the Spanish holiday.</p>
<p>--Jose Barata, Lisbon bureau 3511-3113122</p>
</text>
